Hi!

First of all, thank you all for your answers to questions that have already been asked in the past.

I conducted a CFA to test the structure of a psychological scale, with group = "level of education". The weak invariance or equal factor loadings is not supported (χ2 = 210 (125) vs χ2 = 285 (157), p < .0001).

Consequently, can I still compute the average of my indicators to create my psychological measure? Or would it be better to extract the factor scores, following the procedure Terrence has described there <https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/oKvb2uvAOWo/m/nTKo6KTiDgAJ>, to account for that unequal factor loading depending on the level of education?

Thank you!

