Dear Mike,

That's a good idea. However, what if using different "n"s lead to
different model fits?

Also, when you say "using different sample sizes", what options for
"n" do you have in mind?

For example, in multilevel data, "n" from a study might be like below.
What options for n do we have?

study  groupID  var1      var2                 r        n
1         1             speak    extraversion   .1       35
1          1            writing   extraversion    .2       35
1          2             speak  extraversion     .3       47
1          2             write    extraversion     .4        47

