Jošt Bartol,

I am happy to explain.

I have two CFAs now.

The first CFA is represented by a latent variable "QuantityQuality" or "QQ" for the variation shared among all four indicator variables (v-Loss, intelligence, height, and BMI), and in that CFA I have a 0.99 loading on v-Loss.  So, to answer your question, the latent variable is QuantityQuality or QQ.

The second CFA has two latent variables: QQ1 and QQ2. QQ1 is a latent factor but really just a scaled vLoss, and QQ2 is the latent factor for the variation shared among three variables: intelligence, height, and BMI.  QQ1 and QQ2 correlate with each other by the same value I find in the extreme loading of the first CFA, which seems to validate the result of the first CFA.

Without CFA, I don't think I can get those latent variables.

Abel

